TITLE:: NLMS
summary:: Real-Time Adaptive Normalized Least-Mean-Squares FIR Filter
categories:: UGens>Filters
related:: Guides/Filtra, Classes/ZMorph, Classes/Dispersion

DESCRIPTION::
NLMS is a real-time digital adaptive FIR filter implementing the Normalized Least-Mean-Squares algorithm (Widrow-Hoff / Haykin).

Rather than using fixed frequency response coefficients, NLMS dynamically updates a 32-tap internal transversal filter weight vector at every sample to match an input strong::reference:: signal to a target strong::desired:: signal:
teletype::
e[n] = desired[n] - y[n]
w_k[n+1] = w_k[n] + \frac{\mu}{\epsilon + ||x||^2} \cdot e[n] \cdot x[n-k]
::

NLMS is a dual-output UGen returning:
LIST::
## strong::Output 0::: The estimated signal code::y[n]:: (the adapted FIR output tracking the target).
## strong::Output 1::: The residual error code::e[n]:: (the difference / cancelled output).
::

Applications include real-time acoustic echo and noise cancellation, adaptive inverse modeling, line enhancement, and dynamic resonance suppression.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: ar

ARGUMENT:: reference
Audio-rate input signal driving the adaptive FIR transversal delay line.

ARGUMENT:: desired
Audio-rate target signal that the filter attempts to track or cancel.

ARGUMENT:: mu
Adaptation step size parameter in [0.0, 1.0]. Larger values adapt faster but may increase steady-state misadjustment. Set to 0.0 to freeze filter weights. Default: 0.05.

ARGUMENT:: eps
Regularization constant preventing numerical divergence or division by zero during input silence. Range [1e-6, 1.0]. Default: 0.001.

returns:: An array of two audio-rate signals: code::[estimatedSignal, residualError]::.

EXAMPLES::

CODE::
s.boot;

// 1. Acoustic System Identification & Echo Cancellation
(
x = {
    var ref = PinkNoise.ar(0.3);
    var target = CombN.ar(ref, 0.02, [0.003, 0.007], 0.2).sum * 0.5;
    var sigs = NLMS.ar(ref, target, mu: 0.1, eps: 0.001);
    var estimated = sigs[0];
    var residualError = sigs[1];

    // Left channel: original target; Right channel: noise-cancelled residual error
    [target, residualError] * 0.4;
}.play;
)
::
